{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/850377-question-on-the-old-wyrm","id":850377,"title":"Question on the old wyrm","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-03-20T19:48:23-07:00","id":850377,"title":"Question on the old wyrm","content":"Has anyone run a game where an aspect of the old wyrm was present? Like a wyrm spirit that is still doing its job cleansing the broken creations of the wyld and weaver rather than perpetuating them, and is unaware of/is trying to reverse the wyrms fall to corruption.<br /> <br /> Seems like it would be one hell of a head scratcher if a garou pack found a spirit that smelled wyrmish but at the same time &quot;Different&quot; and was carrying out a role Beneficial to gaia(like a fungal spirit that was cleaning sewers by feeding on the chemicals and wyrm taint)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-20T20:09:15-07:00","id":850381,"title":"","content":"In Rage Across Egypt they have &quot;proto-banes&quot;, spirits of the old wyrm of balance. They mention how the Mokole consider one of them a delicacy. I've ran them a few times in my games, people actually saw them as a sign of hope.<br /> <br /> I also kicked around an idea for my current game of having the Ratkin be more of the old wyrm then of the wyld, since their actual purpose was controlling humanity's population and killing where needed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-21T01:25:23-07:00","id":850450,"title":"","content":"The Wyrm ends everything, not just broken creations. And of course there is still a lot of that going on, I mean Death still exists and while the Wyrm also corrupts it never stopped killing/destroying - and neither do it's spirit servants. And sure, I have all stuff associated with Death and destruction also have Wyrm Taint, that can be detected with the appropriate gift.<br /> <br /> A LARP ST came up with a setting in which an area had three caerns some centuries back, each one dedicated to one aspect of the Triat. The wyrm-ish death oriented caern was sealed, however. The wyld one then in modern times went crazy, using the material from Book of the Wyld. In the end the Death caern was re-established for the players, while the two others were destroyed.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-21T04:34:28-07:00","id":850491,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/850377-question-on-the-old-wyrm#post850377\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Has anyone run a game where an aspect of the old wyrm was present? Like a wyrm spirit that is still doing its job cleansing the broken creations of the wyld and weaver rather than perpetuating them, and is unaware of/is trying to reverse the wyrms fall to corruption.<br /> <br /> Seems like it would be one hell of a head scratcher if a garou pack found a spirit that smelled wyrmish but at the same time &quot;Different&quot; and was carrying out a role Beneficial to gaia(like a fungal spirit that was cleaning sewers by feeding on the chemicals and wyrm taint)</div> </div> </div> </div>If all of the Wyrm was truly and utterly corrupted it wouldn't be doing its day to day job. And it still does, quite admirably. There is death, there is rebirth, there is wear and tear, there is change. That's where the whole philosophy of curing/saving Wyrm comes from. So, yeah it's quite plausible there are uncorrupted spirits doing their job. But if they're doing it right, you'll never really meet them :P","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-21T05:12:05-07:00","id":850504,"title":"","content":"Not sure if tear, wear and rebirth are part of the Wyrm.<br /> <br /> I mean, as the story goes, the Wyrm is still trying to end things, but now he wants to destroy all by corrupting things, so Creation will at some point just break apart, if there is enough corrupted stuff upsetting the balance.<br /> But, and here it is a real philosophical analysis, wear and tear are not complete endings, therefore they are akin to corruption. In the world before the Wyrm went mad, everything was fine and at it's peak<i>, </i>until it ended. We don't know if concepts like old age and 'worn' already existed. For, the Wyld created and the Weaver made static. The Wyrm just ended things. So, what would have made a person or object tear? If the Summer Country is the closest resemblance one has to the Dawn Times, then all plants and all animals wear adult and healthy and even if injured or eaten, returned the next day in exactly that state. Existing in a state less than perfect is something that is corrupt....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-21T09:35:49-07:00","id":850619,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/850377-question-on-the-old-wyrm?p=850504#post850504\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not sure if tear, wear and rebirth are part of the Wyrm.<br /> I mean, as the story goes, the Wyrm is still trying to end things, but now he wants to destroy all by corrupting things, so Creation will at some point just break apart, if there is enough corrupted stuff upsetting the balance.<br /> But, and here it is a real philosophical analysis, wear and tear are not complete endings, therefore they are akin to corruption. In the world before the Wyrm went mad, everything was fine and at it's peak<i>, </i>until it ended. We don't know if concepts like old age and 'worn' already existed. For, the Wyld created and the Weaver made static. The Wyrm just ended things. So, what would have made a person or object tear? If the Summer Country is the closest resemblance one has to the Dawn Times, then all plants and all animals wear adult and healthy and even if injured or eaten, returned the next day in exactly that state. Existing in a state less than perfect is something that is corrupt....</div> </div> </div> </div>Depends on how you look at it. I tend to look at things as the Wyld and weaver Both create things, but not directly. The wyld introduces random change and the weaver collects, modifies and &quot;Perfects&quot; things that already exist. The problem is Most changes are detrimental to anythings that exists(mutations more often than not create genetic disorders and the ones that are helpful are the exception, not the rule.), so in a world where only the weaver and wyld existed everything would slowly become turn into a dysfunctional mess as the wyld kept corrupting things that would have been perfectly functional otherwise and the weaver kept throwing away things it didn't need anymore in favor of the newest creation of the day.<br /> <br /> That's where the wyrm's job makes the most sense, it lives to break down the dysfunctional and used up creations of the weaver and wyld into their base parts so that the cycle of creation can continue unhindered. It is the fungus that eats dead logs and returns their nutrients to the soil, the bacteria that cleans excess chemicals out of the water, and the black hole that reduces particles to usable energy. That is, until it was trapped in a slice of calcified reality by the weaver and the hydra heads of the false wyrm grew over its prison like poisonous mushrooms.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-22T08:29:23-07:00","id":851154,"title":"","content":"I'm in a game right now playing someone who is consecrated of the <i>Defiler Wyrm</i> but wants to serve what he calls the <i>Primal Wyrm</i>, the original form that decided and enforced <i>That Which Should Not Be</i>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3197-david-michael-felt","name":"David Michael Felt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3197_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"42"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}